<%#
  The milestone ladder (v1-scope §7). Each state names the NEXT milestone and
  when to expect it, and none of them ever claims a job ran — §11 rejects the
  deploy-time "preview ping" precisely because a green row for a job that has
  never reported is the lie this product exists not to tell. The first real
  check-in is the demo.

  Wrapped in its own dom_id so Project::MonitorSync can replace it over Turbo
  when a sync commits: without that broadcast, newly-registered monitors appear
  only on reload and the user watching this page sees nothing happen at the exact
  moment it did.

  Locals: project.
%>
<div id="<%= dom_id(project, :setup_milestones) %>" class="mt-6 pt-5 border-t border-hairline"
     data-testid="setup-milestones">
  <% if project.awaiting_first_sync? %>
    <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-ink">
      <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-pending-dot"></span>
      Waiting for your first sync
    </p>
    <p class="text-[12px] text-muted mt-1 ml-3.5">
      Your jobs appear here the moment a deploy runs the command — usually within seconds of it finishing.
    </p>

  <% elsif project.awaiting_first_check_in? %>
    <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-ink" data-testid="milestone-registered">
      <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-pending-dot"></span>
      <%= pluralize(project.monitors.size, "monitor") %> registered — waiting for first check-ins
    </p>
    <p class="text-[12px] text-muted mt-1 ml-3.5">
      Each one turns green the first time that job actually runs. Nothing is wrong until a job misses its window.
    </p>

  <% else %>
    <p class="flex items-center gap-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-up-text" data-testid="milestone-checked-in">
      <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-up-dot"></span>
      Checking in
    </p>
    <p class="text-[12px] text-muted mt-1 ml-3.5">
      This project is live. You'll get an email if a job stops reporting.
    </p>
  <% end %>
</div>
